'' A ustring chain that renders a number, with a narrow or wide term beside it -- 'return k &
'' right( "abc", 2 ) & sp', 'v = 5 & bs & sp' over a narrow bs, 'k & wstr( "wd" ) & sp'. Every
'' term converts to UTF-16, as fbc does (lines measured). LowerUStrInPlaceWithNumbers_
'' converted only the numbers: the narrow bytes were read as UTF-16 ("bc" as U+6362; a one-
'' character term survived by accident), and a wide term stopped the build (TKO0994).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/ustr-chain-narrow-terms.bas -o tests/codegen/ustrchainnarrowterms.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/ustrchainnarrowterms.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/ustrchainnarrowterms.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: A:7bytesS|7bcS|7UXVS|7xvS|7ABS
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: B:755S|7wdS|7ABS7FF|S7bytesxy|7uxvS3.5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: V:5bytesS
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: V:5bcS
